      "side": 1,
      "message": "This prop is for modules which embeds ApexModuleBase and can be part of mainline modules(APEX).\nThe main purpose is to let module authors know that the module should work with \"min_sdk_version\".\nThe default implementation of ShouldSupportSdkVersion relies on min_sdk_version property, but can be overridden by those module which have its own property or different version scheme (e.g. java_library)\n\nFor native modules, this looks like duplicate. But the purpose is a bit different.\nFor example, libbase for com.android.art is built against liblog(30) while libbase for com.android.media is built against liblog(29). libbase may have \"min_sdk_version: 29\" in this case, but it doesn\u0027t necessarily mean it is always built against 29.\n(Note, 29 or 30 here refer the API level of APEX stubs.)",
